{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q018_tal_effector_repeat_lengths\",\"answer\":\"In SCOPe 2.08, d2kq5a_, d3v6pa_, and d4cj9a_ are all classified as domains in the same family a.298.1.1, “TAL (transcription activator-like) effector” (SUNID 267609), within superfamily a.298.1, “TAL effector-like” (SUNID 267596), fold a.298, “Left-handed alpha-alpha superhelix” (SUNID 267589), and class a, “All alpha proteins” (SUNID 46456). The sequence-length mismatch is expected because SCOPe is treating this as a repeat family: the conserved structural/evolutionary unit is a small TAL alpha-helical repeat in a left-handed alpha-alpha superhelix, while different deposited chains contain different numbers of that repeat. SCOPe explicitly marks d2kq5a_ and d3v6pa_ with the repeat-family heterogeneity code `re`, defined for families in which “the common domain is composed of a different number of small repeating units”, and records the canonical repeat representative as 4cj9 A:259-292 from d4cj9a_; for d2kq5a_ the entry also notes “single repeat”. Thus the three SIDs are not being asserted to have equal full-chain lengths or one-to-one repeat counts: d2kq5a_ is PthA, d3v6pa_ is dHax3, and d4cj9a_ is BurrH, but each is an example of the homologous TAL-effector repeat architecture represented by family a.298.1.1. The d4cj9 A:259-292 coordinate is a family representative for the repeat; SCOPe reports that it applies directly to d4cj9a_ and is only a canonical representative for d2kq5a_ and d3v6pa_, so those coordinates must not be transferred as exact boundaries for the other two domains.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"get_scop_domains\",\"/api/v1/releases/current\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/parents\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/annotations\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/homology\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/parents\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/annotations\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/homology\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/parents\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/annotations\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/homology\"]}]}"}}
